{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01MJT5KQYCGUtMR8XQbuhCXN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Anchor** is a single-user personal productivity system for J.C. Liechty, living entirely in `C:\\dev\\Anchor` (no syncing, no siblings; markdown files are the source of truth).\n\n- **Purpose â€” a GTD-style task/project manager.** It tracks tasks and projects across life domains (academic, commercial, family, writing) through a lifecycle (active â†’ done â†’ cancelled â†’ saved-for-later â†’ restored), backed by plain-markdown files (`DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, `domains/*.md`) with no database and no external dependencies (Python stdlib only).\n\n- **What it ships #1 â€” a persistent local web app (`anchor_gui.py`).** A self-contained stdlib HTTP server bound to `http://localhost:8777`, run as the always-on NSSM Windows service `anchor`. It serves an interactive browser dashboard that reads/writes the markdown directly via `/api/*` endpoints (mark done, add, capture, edit, cancel, save, restore). This is the declared deliverable and the primary interface.\n\n- **What it ships #2 â€” a CLI engine (`anchor.py`).** Mirrors the GUI's logic for command-line use (`done`/`add`/`capture`/`cancel`/`save`/`restore`/`dashboard`) and regenerates the static `dashboard.html` fallback.\n\n- **What it ships #3 â€” a daily self-test (`anchor_healthcheck.py`).** Runs at 5:00 AM via Task Scheduler, verifies file integrity, exercises every endpoint on a throwaway port, walks tasks through every state, and writes dated reports to `health_reports/`; failures surface as a red dashboard banner.\n\n- **Its major add-on â€” an R&D \"control surface\" (v2 â†’ v3 â†’ v4), now merged to master.** This turns each project into a **cockpit for \"trio\"-driven R&D work** (the researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman skill pipeline). It provides:\n  - Per-project windows with lane tiles (Research Â· Planning Â· Build Â· Deliverables Â· Grass) each showing one honest status light and an inline expanding panel.\n  - Real **ConPTY interactive terminals** (xterm.js over a hand-rolled WebSocket/SSE transport) with per-session **git-worktree isolation**, where a new session auto-loads the lane's skill once and greets once.\n  - Cached, validated session/project **summaries** (generate-twice + grounding filter), an engine toggle (Claude â†” Gemini), cost/tokens/time rollups, grass-idea promotion, and type-aware deliverable launching.\n  - The lone waiver to the stdlib-only rule: optional `pywinpty` for the terminal subsystem (lazy-imported, degrades gracefully if absent).\n\n- **Branding.** Presented as a Ghost World Labs tool \"Powered by NextGen Nuclear â˜¢.\"\n\nNote: a couple of these claims (R&D surface module roles, endpoints) come from CLAUDE.md documentation rather than re-verified source â€” if you want any specific claim checked against the actual code, I can confirm it."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4410,"cache_read_input_tokens":45325,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4410,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"53054a51-b4a6-42e2-a730-8c71e1981088","uuid":"cf6d4f7f-98d5-4334-ae53-70e83fb49dc5","request_id":"req_011Cc1hskYe1pQWe4R1oUvpb"}
